message: >-
  If you use this work in your research, please cite the preprint below.
title: "Fractal Intelligence: Conceptual Decomposition as Problem-Solving Infrastructure"
abstract: >-
  Fractal intelligence is a form of cumulative intelligence in which bounded,
  concept-defined units recursively decompose and reframe problems, compose
  child work into higher-level capabilities, and preserve evaluated structures
  for reuse or revision across problems, domains, and scales. The paper develops
  one Solver-based realization in which a problem first ascends through adjacent
  abstractions to a root before its specific capability is decomposed. A
  100-problem construction probes whether the resulting topology can be
  instantiated and structurally checked; it does not test solution quality.
